      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Query Scope**\n\nI'm focusing on defining the scope of the Python file, `query_metric_window.py`. The core function will query recent data points for a specific metric over a defined time window. I'm now thinking about selecting a concrete external provider for managed metrics monitoring. Right now, I'm considering Google as a common and feasible choice.\n\n\n**Implementing the Cloud Client**\n\nI've decided to proceed with Google Cloud Monitoring and will integrate the `google.cloud.monitoring_v3` library. The `query_metric_window.py` file is under construction, and I'm importing the necessary modules and laying out the basic function structure. The parameters will be project ID, metric type, an end time, and a duration in minutes. I am currently focusing on building the query using the `MetricServiceClient`.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789867508748,
          "start": 1789867506488
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc6abb38001rbBw3V6rKhUq3q",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc6ab630001LT1KmeQemQwjhR",
      "session_id": "ses_f43954a48ffeCDB8eJk4JL7NZl",
      "time_created": 1789867506488,
      "time_updated": 1789867508748
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "vjfXNRAMkvcGz9Hi",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import os\nfrom google.cloud import monitoring_v3\nfrom google.protobuf import timestamp_pb2\n\ndef query_metric_window(project_id: str, metric_type: str, end_time: int, minutes_ago: int):\n    client = monitoring_v3.MetricServiceClient()\n    project_name = f\"projects/{project_id}\"\n\n    now = timestamp_pb2.Timestamp()\n    now.seconds = end_time\n    \n    interval = monitoring_v3.TimeInterval(\n        end_time=now,\n        start_time=timestamp_pb2.Timestamp(seconds=now.seconds - (minutes_ago * 60)),\n    )\n\n    query = f\"\"\"\n    fetch gce_instance\n    | metric {metric_type}\n    | align delta(1m)\n    | every 1m\n    | group_by [], [value_mean: mean(value.double_value)]\n    \"\"\"\n\n    results = client.query_time_series(\n        name=project_name,\n        query=query,\n        interval=interval,\n    )\n\n    return results\n\n",
            "filePath": "query_metric_window.py"
          },
